Date: Thu, 6 Nov 2026 20:09:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: do not promote unused-symbol warnings to errors

libubox hardcodes -Werror in two independent places, and ADD_DEFINITIONS
appends to the compile line *after* the flags OpenWrt passes via
TARGET_CFLAGS. That means a -Wno-error=... in the package Makefile is
always overridden by the later -Werror, so the only reliable fix is to
remove it at the source:

  CMakeLists.txt:7      ADD_DEFINITIONS(-Wall -Werror)
  lua/CMakeLists.txt:9  ADD_DEFINITIONS(-Os -Wall -Werror --std=gnu99 ...)

The second one is what actually compiles lua/uloop.c.

With GCC 13/14 (Ubuntu 24.04) that file now trips -Wunused-function and
-Wunused-const-variable for symbols that are only reachable when a newer
Lua API is detected, so the build aborts with
"cc1: all warnings being treated as errors". GCC 12 (the CI image) did not
diagnose those cases, which is why this fails only locally.

Targeted -Werror=... options for real defects (implicit-function-declaration,
format-security) are deliberately kept.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 
 PROJECT(ubox C)
 
-ADD_DEFINITIONS(-Wall -Werror)
+ADD_DEFINITIONS(-Wall)
 IF(CMAKE_C_COMPILER_VERSION VERSION_GREATER 6)
 	ADD_DEFINITIONS(-Wextra -Werror=implicit-function-declaration)
 	ADD_DEFINITIONS(-Wformat -Werror=format-security)
--- a/lua/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/lua/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 	pkg_search_module(LUA lua5.1 lua-5.1)
 ENDIF()
 
-ADD_DEFINITIONS(-Os -Wall -Werror --std=gnu99 -g3 -I.. ${LUA_CFLAGS})
+ADD_DEFINITIONS(-Os -Wall --std=gnu99 -g3 -I.. ${LUA_CFLAGS})
 LINK_DIRECTORIES(${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/..)
 
 IF(APPLE)
